<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heraclius the Elder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 610</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> the Elder was a Byzantine general of Armenian origin who served against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> and became Exarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>. In 608 he rebelled against the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocas">Phocas</a>, sending his son Heraclius by sea and his nephew Nicetas overland to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. His son took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and became emperor in 610, shortly before the elder Heraclius died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heraclius-the-elder.jpg" alt="Heraclius the Elder" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Revolt_of_the_Heraclii_solidus_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
